WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
In English, you turn "quick"
into "quickly" by adding "-ly".

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.510
Spanish has its own
ending for that: -mente.

3
00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:13.330
So Sam takes rápido, "quick",
and writes rápidomente.

4
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.690
It looks logical.

5
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:18.050
But a Spanish speaker would
spot a problem straight away.

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.070
What has Sam missed?

7
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.410
In this mission, you'll build
adverbs that say how you do

8
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.070
things, and learn common ones
whole, like a menudo, "often".

9
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.910
You'll sort out "good" from "well",

10
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.650
and join your sentences with
connectives like pero and aunque.

11
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:40.350
Your mission: find out what
Sam missed in rápidomente.
